xnu 0254: deliver a touch position every vsync, and drain what the part has

The lock screen redraws once per touch event. Measured with glframes=1 and
mondrianfb_fps=1 in the same boot, panel swaps and reports read agree one for
one: 32 swaps in the second the part answered 32 reports, 7 in the second it
answered 7, 3 in the second it answered 3, and the frames that arrive with no
touch draw in bursts of 11-17 ms apart (60 fps). So the UI was not slow, it was
starved of positions: the part reports at about 100 Hz and this thread is woken
once a vsync and read exactly one report a wakeup.

Two changes: drain whatever the part has queued (the IRQ line stays low until a
zero byte is written back, so read until it is high, four reports a tick at
most), and, on a tick with no new report while a finger is down, send the last
position again. The second is what makes a drag a 60 Hz stream of positions
instead of whatever rate the part happened to answer at; the window server
coalesces repeated moves. bsd/dev/mondrian_touch.c, and the fps line prints the
re-sent moves as rep N/s.
